LINE 34       "he listed station, offered as a set of temperature ranges plus \u201cor above\u201d / \u201cor below\u201d levels.\\u003cbr\\u003e\",\"class\":\"no-margin\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"text\":\"These markets settle the next morning based on the high temperature recorded in the final NWS Daily Climate Report. Market determination may be delayed in the rare instances of a) a high temperature is not consistent with 6-hr or 24-hr highs reported by METAR or b) the final NWS Climate Report high temperature value is lower than previous preliminary report.\\u003cbr\\u003e\u200b\",\"class\":\"no-margin\"},{\"type\":\"subheading3\",\"text\":\"Hourly Temperature Markets\",\"idAttribute\":\"h_e3c3987fb7\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"text\":\"Some temperature markets are hourly - the market title names an exact time, for example \u201cChicago temperature at 5 PM EDT.\u201d These markets are also directional: each contract resolves on whether the temperature at that time is above or below a specific level, rather than within a range. They settle on the temperature at that exact time as reported by The Weather Company for the station coordinates named in the market rules (for example, KORD for Chicago).\\u003cbr\\u003e\u200b\",\"class\":\"no-margin\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"text\":\"For these markets, The Weather Company\u2019s reported value is official and final. NWS Climatological Reports, Google Weather, and other services may be useful references, but they are not authoritative for settlement. Preliminary Weather Company readings may differ from the final reported value due to roun",
